## Pull request overview

This work-in-progress PR implements mobile-first responsive layouts across ObjectUI's plugin ecosystem and console application, addressing items P5.1 (Plugin Views) and P5.2 (Console Pages) from the roadmap. The changes introduce a new `@object-ui/mobile` package providing touch gesture utilities (pull-to-refresh, swipe detection) and implement mobile-optimized UI patterns including snap-scrolling carousels, card-view fallbacks, touch-friendly controls, and responsive breakpoint-based layouts.

**Changes:**
- Adds `@object-ui/mobile` package dependency to plugin-timeline with pull-to-refresh functionality
- Implements mobile-responsive patterns across 9 plugins (Grid, Kanban, Timeline, Map, Calendar, Gantt, Dashboard, Charts, Detail) including touch targets, responsive padding, column hiding, and layout adaptations
- Enhances console UI with swipe gestures, bottom navigation bar, full-screen mobile dialogs, and responsive text sizing

### Reviewed changes

