The `handleRefresh` function does not return a Promise as expected by the `usePullToRefresh` hook's `onRefresh` callback. The hook expects `onRefresh: () => Promise<void>`, but `handleRefresh` only updates state synchronously. This may cause the pull-to-refresh indicator to not properly track the async operation. Consider making `handleRefresh` async and awaiting any data fetching operation, or explicitly return a resolved Promise.
```suggestion
  const handleRefresh = useCallback((): Promise<void> => {
    setRefreshKey(k => k + 1);
    return Promise.resolve();
```

The resize event listener is added without any throttling or debouncing, which can cause excessive re-renders on window resize. Consider using a debounced or throttled version of the `checkMobile` function to improve performance, especially on lower-end devices where resize events can fire very frequently.
```suggestion
      let resizeTimeout: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null = null;

      const checkMobile = () => {
        setIsMobile(window.innerWidth < 640);
      };

      const handleResize = () => {
        if (resizeTimeout) {
          clearTimeout(resizeTimeout);
        }
        resizeTimeout = setTimeout(checkMobile, 150);
      };

      checkMobile();
      window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);

      return () => {
        if (resizeTimeout) {
          clearTimeout(resizeTimeout);
        }
        window.removeEventListener('resize', handleResize);
      };
```

The auto-switch to day view on mobile happens without notifying the user. When users rotate their device or resize the browser window below 640px, the view suddenly changes from month/week to day view. This can be disorienting. Consider adding a visual notification (toast/snackbar) or maintaining the user's view preference if they've manually selected it, only auto-switching on initial mount.
```suggestion
    // Auto-switch to day view on mobile only on initial mount
    if (typeof window === "undefined") return
    const mq = window.matchMedia("(max-width: 639px)")
    if (mq.matches) {
      setSelectedView("day")
      onViewChangeRef.current?.("day")
    }
```
